  "term": "ventral tegmental area",
  "definition": "The ventral tegmental area is a part of the midbrain located near the substantia nigra and below the red nucleus. It is a major source of dopamine pathways that project to areas including the nucleus accumbens, and increased activity here has been suspected to play a role in the positive symptoms of schizophrenia.",
